# storaged reads eMMC health counters under debugfs (/sys/kernel/debug/mmc0)
# at every boot, and this image does not let it: the counters are nothing the
# system acts on here, and the read is refused four lines into every boot log
# (seen again on the release image, 2026-11-04). Refused on purpose, and not
# written down -- a denial that is known and harmless is noise in the one log
# a reader will send in.
#
# In the platform-private directory, not device/amazon/pw3/sepolicy: storaged
# is a private platform type (system/sepolicy/private/storaged.te) and the
# vendor policy cannot name it (checkpolicy: unknown type storaged, 2026-11-04).
dontaudit storaged debugfs_mmc:dir search;
dontaudit storaged debugfs_mmc:file read;
